            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0410" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/2217: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-16T15:00:00+08:00">December 16, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1162. Referring to my 1156, December 15, 9 p.m.,<anchor n="44" xml:id="d496-f1"/>
                    the First Secretary of the Japanese Embassy informed this office this morning
                    that according to reports from the Japanese military in Nanking the 18 Americans
                    who remained in that city are well and uninjured and that the Embassy buildings
                    were not damaged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
